      "title": "Files and Modules at a Glance",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Files and Modules at a Glance",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Files",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`open()` returns a ==file object== tied to an **OS file handle**",
                "`with open(p) as f:` ==closes== the file on exit, even on error"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mode",
                "Gives",
                "Bytes decoded?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Text (`'r'`)",
                  "`str`",
                  "Yes, pass `encoding='utf-8'`"
                ],
                [
                  "Binary (`'rb'`)",
                  "`bytes`",
                  "No, raw"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Modules and Packages",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==module== is one `.py` file",
                "A ==package== is a folder of modules",
                "Import runs the module **once**, then caches it in `sys.modules`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "import m",
                    "sub": "first request",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Run file once",
                    "sub": "top to bottom",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "sys.modules",
                    "sub": "cached object",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "import m again",
                    "sub": "reuses cache",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. venv and pip",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`venv` gives each project its own ==interpreter== and `site-packages`",
                "`pip` installs into the ==active== environment only"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "python -m venv .venv",
                "source .venv/bin/activate",
                "python -m pip install requests"
              ],
              "note": "Windows activate: .venv\\Scripts\\activate"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Activate first, or pip installs into the **wrong** Python. Never commit `.venv`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "open(), Modes and Encoding",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "open(), Modes and Encoding",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Mode Letters",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mode",
                "Does",
                "File missing"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`r`",
                  "read (==default==)",
                  "error"
                ],
                [
                  "`w`",
                  "truncate and write",
                  "created"
                ],
                [
                  "`a`",
                  "append at end",
                  "created"
                ],
                [
                  "`x`",
                  "create only",
                  "{red:fails if it exists}"
                ],
                [
                  "`+`",
                  "read and write",
                  "per base letter"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`t` = text (default): `'r'` returns ==str==",
                "`b` = binary: `'rb'` returns ==bytes==",
                "Combine: `'rb'`, `'w+'`, `'ab'`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Encoding and Newlines",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Always pass ==encoding='utf-8'== in text mode",
                "Default is **platform dependent**, often cp1252 on Windows",
                "Text mode translates newlines; use ==newline=''== for csv"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "with open('rows.csv', 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:",
                "    f.write('a,b\\n')"
              ],
              "note": "csv files: utf-8 and newline=''"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "w erases on open",
              "text": "`'w'` truncates the file at ==open time==, before any write. Use `'a'` to keep existing content."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why pass encoding?** The default differs by OS, so output differs",
                "**w vs a?** w wipes the file on open; a appends",
                "**x mode?** Creates the file, raises if it exists"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "with Blocks and Reading Patterns",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "with Blocks and Reading Patterns",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The with Block",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`with open(p) as f:` calls ==f.close()== on exit",
                "Closes even when an {red:exception} is raised",
                "Open two files in one statement, comma-separated"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "with open(a) as src, open(b, 'w') as dst:",
                "    for line in src:",
                "        dst.write(line)"
              ],
              "note": "both files closed on exit"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Reading Patterns",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Returns",
                "Memory"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`for line in f`",
                  "one line per step",
                  "{green:constant}"
                ],
                [
                  "`f.readline()`",
                  "one line",
                  "one line"
                ],
                [
                  "`f.read(n)`",
                  "a chunk of n",
                  "n"
                ],
                [
                  "`f.readlines()`",
                  "list of all lines",
                  "{red:everything}"
                ],
                [
                  "`f.read()`",
                  "one string",
                  "{red:everything}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Newlines",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Lines keep their trailing ==\\n==",
                "Strip it with `line.rstrip('\\n')`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "with open(p, encoding='utf-8') as f:",
                "    for line in f:",
                "        line = line.rstrip('\\n')"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Big files",
              "text": "Loop over ==for line in f==. `read()` and `readlines()` load the whole file."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
