              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A script runs `open('app.log', 'w')` to add one more line to a 50-line log. What does the file hold afterwards?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Only the new line: `w` truncates at open time.",
                "Use `'a'` to keep existing content."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Your project has a file `random.py` and a script with `import random; random.randint(1, 6)`. Why does it fail?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Your local file shadows the stdlib module, so it has no `randint`.",
                "Rename the file."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`helper.py` contains `print('loaded')`. How many times is it printed by the code below?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Once: the first import runs the module and caches it in `sys.modules`.",
                "The second import reuses the cache."
              ],
